  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="sp-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h2">
    <div class="sp-faq-inner">
      <p class="sp-section-label">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="sp-section-h2" id="faq-h2">Brick &amp; Stone Veneers FAQ<br><em>Answered Honestly</em></h2>
      <div class="sp-faq-list" role="list">

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-1">
            What's the difference between full-thickness masonry and veneer?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-1" role="region">
            <p>Full-thickness masonry (like a full brick wall) is structural — it carries load. Veneer is a facing material attached to a substrate — it's not structural. Veneer is lighter and faster to install, but requires a correct substrate system to last. AMS installs both.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-2">
            Is brick veneer as durable as full brick?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-2" role="region">
            <p>Properly installed brick veneer — with correct waterproofing, lath, scratch coat, and movement joints — lasts as long as full brick. The failure mode for veneer is almost always the substrate system, not the brick itself.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-3">
            Can veneer be installed on any wall?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-3" role="region">
            <p>Almost any wall can accept veneer with the right substrate prep. We assess each wall before recommending a veneer system — some substrates require reinforcement or additional waterproofing.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-4">
            How thick is brick or stone veneer?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-4" role="region">
            <p>Thin veneer panels are typically 3/4" to 1-1/4" thick. Full veneer (adhered to substrate, not pinned) runs 1-1/4" to 2". AMS installs both thin-set and full-thickness adhered systems.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-5">
            Do I need permits for veneer installation?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-5" role="region">
            <p>In most Chicagoland municipalities, veneer installation on a structure's exterior requires a permit. AMS pulls all required permits and schedules inspections.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-6">
            How long does veneer installation take?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-6" role="region">
            <p>A feature wall or fireplace runs 1–2 days. A partial exterior takes 3–7 days. Full exterior veneer can run 1–3 weeks depending on size and pattern.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-7">
            What maintenance does brick or stone veneer require?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-7" role="region">
            <p>Brick veneer: inspect joints every 5–7 years, repoint any deteriorating areas, keep weep holes clear. Stone veneer: reseal every 5–7 years. Annual visual inspection is recommended in Chicago's climate.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-8">
            Are you licensed and insured for veneer installation?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-8" role="region">
            <p>Yes — licensed in Illinois, $2.5M general liability, workers' comp on all crew. Proof of insurance available before work begins.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

